    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d339">

                <pb facs="0792" n="744" sameAs="frus:frus1868p1/pg744"/>

                <head>Mr. Van Valkenburgh to Mr. Seward.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 53.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Legation of the United States</hi>,
                                <hi rendition="#italic">Yokohama,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1868-05-26"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >May</hi> 26, 1868.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> With reference to my dispatch No. 46, of
                    the 27th ultimo, I now have the honor to transmit herewith No. 1, copy of the
                    affidavit of <pb facs="0793" n="745" xml:id="pg745"/> Captain Jones, master of
                    the American bark Dispatch, and No. 2, copy of my letter on this subject to our
                    consul at Kanagawa, for transmission to the consular agent Mr. Frank, at
                    Hiogo.</p>
                <p>I hope soon to hear, for your information, from our consular agent that this
                    matter has been satisfactorily settled.</p>
                <p>I have the honor to be, sir, very respectfully your most obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>R. B. VAN VALKENBURGH.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>Hon. <hi rendition="#small-caps">William H. Seward</hi>, <hi
                            rendition="#italic">Secretary of State, Washington, D. C.</hi></p>
                </postscript>



                <xi:include href="d339-a1.xml" xpointer="d339-a1"/>
